{"book":"fet-trig","bookTitle":"Trigonometry: ratios and identities","concept":1,"title":"Trig ratios in right triangles","grades":"Grade 10","goal":"I can write down sin, cos and tan of an angle in a right triangle.","teach":"In a right triangle, name the sides from the angle you are using: the <b>hypotenuse</b> is opposite the right angle, the <b>opposite</b> side faces the angle and the <b>adjacent</b> side is next to it. sin = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>opposite</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>hypotenuse</i></span></span>, cos = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>adjacent</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>hypotenuse</i></span></span>, tan = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\"><i>opposite</i></span><span class=\"d\"><i>adjacent</i></span></span> (SOH CAH TOA).","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:286px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 150\"><polygon points=\"25,125 180,125 180,20\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><polyline points=\"168,125 168,113 180,113\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"17.0\" y=\"130.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"130.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"24.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text><text x=\"102.5\" y=\"142.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"76.5\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"92.5\" y=\"66.5\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">10</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">For angle A: opposite BC = 6, adjacent AB = 8, hypotenuse AC = 10.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"In the triangle in Teach, find sin A, cos A and tan A.","steps":["sin A = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>.","cos A = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">8</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>.","tan A = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">8</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span>."]},"watch":"Opposite and adjacent depend on which angle you use; the hypotenuse never changes.","qs":[{"text":"cos A","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"cos A","a":"4/5","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Adjacent over hypotenuse, then simplify.","steps":"1. Formulas (right-angled triangle): sin θ = opposite ÷ hypotenuse; cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse; tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent.<br>2. From A: adjacent = AB = 8, hypotenuse = 10<br>3. cos A = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">8</span><span class=\"d\">10</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>"},{"text":"tan A","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"tan A","a":"3/4","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Opposite over adjacent, then simplify.","steps":"1. Formulas (right-angled triangle): sin θ = opposite ÷ hypotenuse; cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse; tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent.<br>2. From A: opposite = 6, adjacent = 8<br>3. tan A = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">6</span><span class=\"d\">8</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">3</span><span class=\"d\">4</span></span>"},{"text":"tan C","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"tan C","a":"4/3","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"From C: opposite AB.","steps":"1. Formulas (right-angled triangle): sin θ = opposite ÷ hypotenuse; cos θ = adjacent ÷ hypotenuse; tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent.<br>2. From C: opposite = AB = 8, adjacent = BC = 6<br>3. tan C = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">8</span><span class=\"d\">6</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">4</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span>"}]}